@export Under Article 5, as a person affected by an AI system, is the AI practice used on me prohibited by Article 5(1)(g) (biometric categorisation to infer race, political opinions, trade union membership, religious or philosophical beliefs, sex life or sexual orientation)?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the AI system is for the purpose of assigning natural persons to specific categories` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system for the purpose of assigning natural persons to specific categories? (An element of the definition of a biometric categorisation system, Article 3(40).)
      `the AI system assigns natural persons to specific categories on the basis of their biometric data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the AI system assign natural persons to specific categories on the basis of their biometric data? (Article 3(40).)
      `the categorisation is ancillary to another commercial service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the categorisation ancillary to another commercial service? (Article 3(40) leaves out a categorisation that is both ancillary to another commercial service and strictly necessary for objective technical reasons.)
      `the categorisation is strictly necessary for objective technical reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the categorisation strictly necessary for objective technical reasons? (Article 3(40).)
      `the AI system categorises natural persons individually` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the AI system categorise natural persons individually? (Article 5(1), point (g), speaks of systems that categorise individually.)
      `it categorises them to deduce or infer their race, political opinions, trade union membership, religious or philosophical beliefs, sex life or sexual orientation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it categorises them to deduce or infer their race, political opinions, trade union membership, religious or philosophical beliefs, sex life or sexual orientation?
      `the data is personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the data personal data? (An element of the definition of biometric data, Article 3(34).)
      `the data results from specific technical processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the data result from specific technical processing? (Article 3(34).)
      `the data relates to the physical, physiological or behavioural characteristics of a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the data relate to the physical, physiological or behavioural characteristics of a natural person? (Article 3(34).)
      `the system does labelling or filtering of lawfully acquired datasets, such as images` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the system do labelling or filtering of lawfully acquired datasets, such as images?
      `the use is carried out by law enforcement authorities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the use carried out by law enforcement authorities? (An element of the definition of law enforcement, Article 3(46).)
      `the use is carried out on behalf of law enforcement authorities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the use carried out on behalf of law enforcement authorities? (Article 3(46).)
      `the use is for the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including safeguarding against and preventing threats to public security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the use for the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including safeguarding against and preventing threats to public security? (Article 3(46).)
      `the system categorises the data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the system categorise that data?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5, as a person affected by an AI system, is the AI practice used on me prohibited by Article 5(1)(g) (biometric categorisation to infer race, political opinions, trade union membership, religious or philosophical beliefs, sex life or sexual orientation)` IS
    `Art 5(1)(g) the AI practice is prohibited` `the date asked` `Art 5(1) act use` FALSE `the AI system is a biometric categorisation system that categorises individually natural persons based on their biometric data` `it categorises them to deduce or infer their race, political opinions, trade union membership, religious or philosophical beliefs, sex life or sexual orientation` `the system does labelling or filtering of lawfully acquired biometric datasets, such as images, based on biometric data` `the system categorises biometric data in the area of law enforcement`
    WHERE
        `the AI system is a biometric categorisation system that categorises individually natural persons based on their biometric data` MEANS
            (`Art 3(40) the AI system is a biometric categorisation system` TRUE `the AI system is for the purpose of assigning natural persons to specific categories` `the AI system assigns natural persons to specific categories on the basis of their biometric data` `the categorisation is ancillary to another commercial service` `the categorisation is strictly necessary for objective technical reasons`) AND (`the AI system categorises natural persons individually`)
        `the data is biometric data` MEANS
            `Art 3(34) the data is biometric data` `the data is personal data` `the data results from specific technical processing` `the data relates to the physical, physiological or behavioural characteristics of a natural person`
        `the system does labelling or filtering of lawfully acquired biometric datasets, such as images, based on biometric data` MEANS
            (`the system does labelling or filtering of lawfully acquired datasets, such as images`) AND (`the data is biometric data`)
        `the use is for the purposes of law enforcement` MEANS
            `Art 3(46) the activities are law enforcement` `the use is carried out by law enforcement authorities` `the use is carried out on behalf of law enforcement authorities` `the use is for the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including safeguarding against and preventing threats to public security`
        `the system categorises biometric data in the area of law enforcement` MEANS
            (`the system categorises the data`) AND (`the data is biometric data`) AND (`the use is for the purposes of law enforcement`)

@export Under Article 5, as a person affected by an AI system, is the AI practice used on me prohibited by Article 5(1)(h) ('real-time' remote biometric identification in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement)?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the AI system is for the purpose of identifying natural persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system for the purpose of identifying natural persons? (An element of the definition of a remote biometric identification system, Article 3(41).)
      `the AI system identifies natural persons without their active involvement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the AI system identify natural persons without their active involvement? (Article 3(41).)
      `the AI system identifies natural persons through the comparison of a person's biometric data with the biometric data contained in a reference database` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the AI system identify natural persons by comparing a person's biometric data with the biometric data contained in a reference database? (Article 3(41).)
      `the capturing of biometric data, the comparison and the identification all occur without a significant delay, instant or after limited short delays in order to avoid circumvention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the capturing of the biometric data, the comparison and the identification all occur without a significant delay (instantly, or after limited short delays in order to avoid circumvention)? (This is what makes a remote biometric identification system a 'real-time' one, Article 3(42).)
      `the place where the system is used is a physical place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place where the system is used a physical place? (An element of the definition of a publicly accessible space, Article 3(44).)
      `the place where the system is used is accessible to an undetermined number of natural persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place where the system is used accessible to an undetermined number of natural persons? (Article 3(44).)
      `the use is carried out by law enforcement authorities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the use carried out by law enforcement authorities? (An element of the definition of law enforcement, Article 3(46).)
      `the use is carried out on behalf of law enforcement authorities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the use carried out on behalf of law enforcement authorities? (Article 3(46).)
      `the use is for the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including safeguarding against and preventing threats to public security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the use for the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including safeguarding against and preventing threats to public security? (Article 3(46).)
      `the use is strictly necessary for the targeted search for specific victims of abduction, trafficking in human beings or sexual exploitation of human beings, as well as the search for missing persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the use is strictly necessary for the targeted search for specific victims of abduction, trafficking in human beings or sexual exploitation of human beings, as well as the search for missing persons?
      `the use is strictly necessary for the prevention of a specific, substantial and imminent threat to the life or physical safety of natural persons or a genuine and present or genuine and foreseeable threat of a terrorist attack` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the use is strictly necessary for the prevention of a specific, substantial and imminent threat to the life or physical safety of natural persons or a genuine and present or genuine and foreseeable threat of a terrorist attack?
      `the use is strictly necessary for the localisation or identification of a person suspected of having committed a criminal offence, for the purpose of conducting a criminal investigation or prosecution or executing a criminal penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the use is strictly necessary for the localisation or identification of a person suspected of having committed a criminal offence, for the purpose of conducting a criminal investigation or prosecution or executing a criminal penalty?
      `the offence is referred to in Annex II` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the offence is referred to in Annex II?
      `the maximum period of the custodial sentence or detention order for the offence in the Member State concerned, in years` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the longest custodial sentence or detention order, in years, that the offence carries in the Member State concerned? Give 0 if it carries none.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5, as a person affected by an AI system, is the AI practice used on me prohibited by Article 5(1)(h) ('real-time' remote biometric identification in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement)` IS
    `Art 5(1)(h) the AI practice is prohibited` `the date asked` `Art 5(1) act use` `the AI system is a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system` `the system is used in publicly accessible spaces` `the use is for the purposes of law enforcement` `the use is strictly necessary for the targeted search for specific victims of abduction, trafficking in human beings or sexual exploitation of human beings, as well as the search for missing persons` `the use is strictly necessary for the prevention of a specific, substantial and imminent threat to the life or physical safety of natural persons or a genuine and present or genuine and foreseeable threat of a terrorist attack` `the use is strictly necessary for the localisation or identification of a person suspected of having committed a criminal offence, for the purpose of conducting a criminal investigation or prosecution or executing a criminal penalty` `the offence is referred to in Annex II` `the maximum period of the custodial sentence or detention order for the offence in the Member State concerned, in years`
    WHERE
        `the AI system is a remote biometric identification system` MEANS
            `Art 3(41) the AI system is a remote biometric identification system` TRUE `the AI system is for the purpose of identifying natural persons` `the AI system identifies natural persons without their active involvement` `the AI system identifies natural persons through the comparison of a person's biometric data with the biometric data contained in a reference database`
        `the AI system is a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system` MEANS
            `Art 3(42) the AI system is a real-time remote biometric identification system` `the AI system is a remote biometric identification system` `the capturing of biometric data, the comparison and the identification all occur without a significant delay, instant or after limited short delays in order to avoid circumvention`
        `the system is used in publicly accessible spaces` MEANS
            `Art 3(44) the place is a publicly accessible space` `the place where the system is used is a physical place` `the place where the system is used is accessible to an undetermined number of natural persons`
        `the use is for the purposes of law enforcement` MEANS
            `Art 3(46) the activities are law enforcement` `the use is carried out by law enforcement authorities` `the use is carried out on behalf of law enforcement authorities` `the use is for the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including safeguarding against and preventing threats to public security`

§§ `Article 5(3): decisions on the output of the system`

@export Under Article 5, as a person affected by an AI system, is a decision with an adverse legal effect on me barred under Article 5(3) where it rests solely on the output of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the decision produces an adverse legal effect on a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the decision produces an adverse legal effect on a person?
      `the AI system is for the purpose of identifying natural persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system for the purpose of identifying natural persons? (An element of the definition of a remote biometric identification system, Article 3(41).)
      `the AI system identifies natural persons without their active involvement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the AI system identify natural persons without their active involvement? (Article 3(41).)
      `the AI system identifies natural persons through the comparison of a person's biometric data with the biometric data contained in a reference database` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the AI system identify natural persons by comparing a person's biometric data with the biometric data contained in a reference database? (Article 3(41).)
      `the capturing of biometric data, the comparison and the identification all occur without a significant delay, instant or after limited short delays in order to avoid circumvention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the capturing of the biometric data, the comparison and the identification all occur without a significant delay (instantly, or after limited short delays in order to avoid circumvention)? (This is what makes a remote biometric identification system a 'real-time' one, Article 3(42).)
      `the decision is taken based solely on the output of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision taken based solely on the output of the AI system?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5, as a person affected by an AI system, is a decision with an adverse legal effect on me barred under Article 5(3) where it rests solely on the output of a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system` IS
    `Art 5(3) the decision is barred because it produces an adverse legal effect and rests solely on the output` `the date asked` `the decision produces an adverse legal effect on a person` `the decision is taken based solely on the output of the 'real-time' remote biometric identification system`
    WHERE
        `the AI system is a remote biometric identification system` MEANS
            `Art 3(41) the AI system is a remote biometric identification system` TRUE `the AI system is for the purpose of identifying natural persons` `the AI system identifies natural persons without their active involvement` `the AI system identifies natural persons through the comparison of a person's biometric data with the biometric data contained in a reference database`
        `the AI system is a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system` MEANS
            `Art 3(42) the AI system is a real-time remote biometric identification system` `the AI system is a remote biometric identification system` `the capturing of biometric data, the comparison and the identification all occur without a significant delay, instant or after limited short delays in order to avoid circumvention`
        `the decision is taken based solely on the output of the 'real-time' remote biometric identification system` MEANS
            (`the decision is taken based solely on the output of the AI system`) AND (`the AI system is a 'real-time' remote biometric identification system`)

§§ `Article 5(8): other Union law`

@export Under Article 5, as a person affected by an AI system, does Article 5 affect a prohibition that applies to the AI practice used on me under other Union law?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the AI practice infringes other Union law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the AI practice infringes other Union law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 5, as a person affected by an AI system, does Article 5 affect a prohibition that applies to the AI practice used on me under other Union law` IS
    `Art 5(8) Article 5 affects the prohibitions that apply under other Union law` `the date asked` `the AI practice infringes other Union law`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat person from part P2 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P2-seat-person.l4: the seat of a person affected by an AI system, over the layer-1 modules of part P2 (Article 4a, Articles 8 to 15, Annex IV).
-- It calls the layer-1 rules and never restates one. Every question has @export and @desc and takes plain inputs; the records a rule expects are built in a WHERE.
-- The shared inputs have the same names and @desc in every question: the date asked; the route by which the AI system is high-risk; the date it was placed on the market or put into service; whether its design was significantly changed since Chapter III applied.
-- A result of NOTHING is "not covered" (not yet applicable, saved by Article 111(2), or outside what the text says); JUST FALSE is the text's own "no".
-- The seat assumes its role: the person asking holds it (the role question below calls the keel's definition once).

§ `The role and the applicability of the provisions`

@export Under Article 4a, as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as an affected person in the Union?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the person is an affected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person affected by an AI system?
      `the person's place` IS A `Place of a party` @desc Are you established or located in the Union, or in a third country?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4a, as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as an affected person in the Union` IS
    `Art 2(1)(g) the Regulation applies to the affected person in the Union` `the date asked` `the person is an affected person` `the person's place`

@export Under Article 4a, as a person affected by an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4a, as a person affected by an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter I` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)

@export Under Article 8, as a person affected by an AI system, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 8, as a person affected by an AI system, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)


§ `Under Article 4a: processing special categories of personal data for bias detection and correction`

@export Under Article 4a(1), as a person affected by an AI system, may the provider of a high-risk AI system exceptionally process special categories of my personal data to ensure bias detection and correction?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the category is referred to in Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the category of personal data concerned one referred to in Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, religious or philosophical beliefs, trade union membership, genetic or biometric data, health, sex life or sexual orientation)?
      `the category is referred to in Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the category of personal data concerned one referred to in Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680?
      `the category is referred to in Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the category of personal data concerned one referred to in Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725?
      `the party is a provider of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the party that processes the special categories of personal data the provider of the high-risk AI system?
      `the processing is strictly necessary to ensure bias detection and correction in relation to high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 10(2), points (f) and (g)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that the processing is strictly necessary to ensure bias detection and correction in relation to high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 10(2), points (f) and (g)?
      `appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons are in place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons are in place?
      `the provisions set out in Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680, as applicable, are also complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that the provisions set out in Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680, as applicable, are also complied with?
      `the bias detection and correction cannot be effectively fulfilled by processing other data, including synthetic or anonymised data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that the bias detection and correction cannot be effectively fulfilled by processing other data, including synthetic or anonymised data?
      `the special categories of personal data are subject to technical limitations on the re-use of personal data, and state-of-the-art security and privacy-preserving measures, including pseudonymisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that the special categories of personal data are subject to technical limitations on the re-use of personal data, and state-of-the-art security and privacy-preserving measures, including pseudonymisation?
      `the special categories of personal data are subject to measures to ensure that the personal data processed are secured and protected, subject to suitable safeguards, including strict controls and documentation of the access, to avoid misuse and to ensure that only authorised persons have access to those personal data with appropriate confidentiality obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that the special categories of personal data are subject to measures to ensure that the personal data processed are secured and protected, subject to suitable safeguards, including strict controls and documentation of the access, to avoid misuse and to ensure that only authorised persons have access to those personal data with appropriate confidentiality obligations?
      `the special categories of personal data are not transmitted, transferred or otherwise accessed by other parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that the special categories of personal data are not transmitted, transferred or otherwise accessed by other parties?
      `the special categories of personal data are deleted once the bias has been corrected or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period, whichever comes first` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that the special categories of personal data are deleted once the bias has been corrected or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period, whichever comes first?
      `the records of processing activities pursuant to Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680 include the reasons why the processing of special categories of personal data was strictly necessary to detect and correct biases, and why that objective could not be achieved by processing other data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that the records of processing activities pursuant to Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680 include the reasons why the processing of special categories of personal data was strictly necessary to detect and correct biases, and why that objective could not be achieved by processing other data?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4a(1), as a person affected by an AI system, may the provider of a high-risk AI system exceptionally process special categories of my personal data to ensure bias detection and correction` IS
    `Art 4a(1) the provider may exceptionally process special categories of personal data` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the party is a provider of the AI system` (`Art 3(37) the category is a special category of personal data` `the category is referred to in Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679` `the category is referred to in Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680` `the category is referred to in Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725`) `the processing is strictly necessary to ensure bias detection and correction in relation to high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 10(2), points (f) and (g)` `appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons are in place` `the provisions set out in Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680, as applicable, are also complied with` `the bias detection and correction cannot be effectively fulfilled by processing other data, including synthetic or anonymised data` `the special categories of personal data are subject to technical limitations on the re-use of personal data, and state-of-the-art security and privacy-preserving measures, including pseudonymisation` `the special categories of personal data are subject to measures to ensure that the personal data processed are secured and protected, subject to suitable safeguards, including strict controls and documentation of the access, to avoid misuse and to ensure that only authorised persons have access to those personal data with appropriate confidentiality obligations` `the special categories of personal data are not transmitted, transferred or otherwise accessed by other parties` `the special categories of personal data are deleted once the bias has been corrected or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period, whichever comes first` `the records of processing activities pursuant to Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680 include the reasons why the processing of special categories of personal data was strictly necessary to detect and correct biases, and why that objective could not be achieved by processing other data`

@export Under Article 4a(2), as a person affected by an AI system, may a provider or deployer of another AI system or model, or a deployer of a high-risk AI system, exceptionally process special categories of my personal data to ensure bias detection and correction?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the category is referred to in Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the category of personal data concerned one referred to in Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (racial or ethnic origin, political opinions, religious or philosophical beliefs, trade union membership, genetic or biometric data, health, sex life or sexual orientation)?
      `the category is referred to in Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the category of personal data concerned one referred to in Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680?
      `the category is referred to in Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the category of personal data concerned one referred to in Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725?
      `the party is a provider of an AI system or of an AI model other than a high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the party processing your special categories of personal data the provider of an AI system or of an AI model that is not a high-risk AI system?
      `the party is a deployer of an AI system or of an AI model other than a high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the party processing your special categories of personal data a deployer of an AI system or of an AI model that is not a high-risk AI system?
      `the party is a deployer of a high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the party processing your special categories of personal data a deployer of a high-risk AI system?
      `such processing is strictly necessary to ensure bias detection and correction in view of possible biases that are likely to affect the health and safety of persons, have a negative impact on fundamental rights or lead to discrimination prohibited pursuant to Union law, especially where data outputs influence inputs for future operations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that such processing is strictly necessary to ensure bias detection and correction in view of possible biases that are likely to affect the health and safety of persons, have a negative impact on fundamental rights or lead to discrimination prohibited pursuant to Union law, especially where data outputs influence inputs for future operations?
      `appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons are in place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons are in place?
      `the provisions set out in Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680, as applicable, are also complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that the provisions set out in Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680, as applicable, are also complied with?
      `the bias detection and correction cannot be effectively fulfilled by processing other data, including synthetic or anonymised data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that the bias detection and correction cannot be effectively fulfilled by processing other data, including synthetic or anonymised data?
      `the special categories of personal data are subject to technical limitations on the re-use of personal data, and state-of-the-art security and privacy-preserving measures, including pseudonymisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that the special categories of personal data are subject to technical limitations on the re-use of personal data, and state-of-the-art security and privacy-preserving measures, including pseudonymisation?
      `the special categories of personal data are subject to measures to ensure that the personal data processed are secured and protected, subject to suitable safeguards, including strict controls and documentation of the access, to avoid misuse and to ensure that only authorised persons have access to those personal data with appropriate confidentiality obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that the special categories of personal data are subject to measures to ensure that the personal data processed are secured and protected, subject to suitable safeguards, including strict controls and documentation of the access, to avoid misuse and to ensure that only authorised persons have access to those personal data with appropriate confidentiality obligations?
      `the special categories of personal data are not transmitted, transferred or otherwise accessed by other parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that the special categories of personal data are not transmitted, transferred or otherwise accessed by other parties?
      `the special categories of personal data are deleted once the bias has been corrected or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period, whichever comes first` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that the special categories of personal data are deleted once the bias has been corrected or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period, whichever comes first?
      `the records of processing activities pursuant to Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680 include the reasons why the processing of special categories of personal data was strictly necessary to detect and correct biases, and why that objective could not be achieved by processing other data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, in the processing of your special categories of personal data: is it the case that the records of processing activities pursuant to Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680 include the reasons why the processing of special categories of personal data was strictly necessary to detect and correct biases, and why that objective could not be achieved by processing other data?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 4a(2), as a person affected by an AI system, may a provider or deployer of another AI system or model, or a deployer of a high-risk AI system, exceptionally process special categories of my personal data to ensure bias detection and correction` IS
    `Art 4a(2) the provider or deployer may exceptionally process special categories of personal data` `the date asked` `the party is a provider of an AI system or of an AI model other than a high-risk AI system` `the party is a deployer of an AI system or of an AI model other than a high-risk AI system` `the party is a deployer of a high-risk AI system` (`Art 3(37) the category is a special category of personal data` `the category is referred to in Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679` `the category is referred to in Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680` `the category is referred to in Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725`) `such processing is strictly necessary to ensure bias detection and correction in view of possible biases that are likely to affect the health and safety of persons, have a negative impact on fundamental rights or lead to discrimination prohibited pursuant to Union law, especially where data outputs influence inputs for future operations` `appropriate safeguards for the fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons are in place` `the provisions set out in Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680, as applicable, are also complied with` `the bias detection and correction cannot be effectively fulfilled by processing other data, including synthetic or anonymised data` `the special categories of personal data are subject to technical limitations on the re-use of personal data, and state-of-the-art security and privacy-preserving measures, including pseudonymisation` `the special categories of personal data are subject to measures to ensure that the personal data processed are secured and protected, subject to suitable safeguards, including strict controls and documentation of the access, to avoid misuse and to ensure that only authorised persons have access to those personal data with appropriate confidentiality obligations` `the special categories of personal data are not transmitted, transferred or otherwise accessed by other parties` `the special categories of personal data are deleted once the bias has been corrected or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period, whichever comes first` `the records of processing activities pursuant to Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680 include the reasons why the processing of special categories of personal data was strictly necessary to detect and correct biases, and why that objective could not be achieved by processing other data`

§ `Under Article 14: human oversight`

@export Under Article 14(5), as a person affected by an AI system, if a high-risk AI system referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III identifies me, is the deployer barred from taking an action or decision about me on the basis of that identification?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights than the requirement or obligation this question is about? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would limiting the application of the requirement or obligation this question is about leave the overall level of protection provided by this Regulation undiminished? Answer no if you do not know.
      `the high-risk AI system is referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the high-risk AI system one referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III (a remote biometric identification system, not one used only for biometric verification to confirm that a specific natural person is who they claim to be)?
      `the high-risk AI system is used for the purposes of law enforcement, migration, border control or asylum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, is it the case that the high-risk AI system is used for the purposes of law enforcement, migration, border control or asylum?
      `Union or national law considers the application of the requirement for a separate verification to be disproportionate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, is it the case that Union or national law considers the application of the requirement for a separate verification to be disproportionate?
      `the identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons with the necessary competence, training and authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As far as you know, is it the case that the identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons with the necessary competence, training and authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 14(5), as a person affected by an AI system, if a high-risk AI system referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III identifies me, is the deployer barred from taking an action or decision about me on the basis of that identification` IS
    `Art 14(5) the deployer is barred from taking an action or decision on the basis of the identification` `the date asked` `the AI system as stated` `the harmonisation facts as stated` `the high-risk AI system is referred to in point 1(a) of Annex III` `the high-risk AI system is used for the purposes of law enforcement, migration, border control or asylum` `Union or national law considers the application of the requirement for a separate verification to be disproportionate` `the identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons with the necessary competence, training and authority`
    WHERE
        `the AI system as stated` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
        `the harmonisation facts as stated` MEANS `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts` WITH
            `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
            `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned`
            `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat person from part P3 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P3-seat-person: the questions of Articles 16 to 27 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744), asked as a person affected by an AI system
-- A thin layer: every question calls one decision function of the layer-1 modules and restates no rule. The inputs that all questions of this part share carry the same name and the same description in every question.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words; NOTHING the text does not answer (the provision does not yet apply, the list is not closed, the provision limits itself, or the text points outside the sources).
-- The role questions and the applicability question come first; a caller that is not sure of the role asks the role question before the duty questions.

§ `Does the Regulation apply on the date asked`

@export Under Article 16, as a person affected by an AI system, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under Article 16, as a person affected by an AI system, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked` MEANS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)

§ `Which party am I`

@export Under Article 16, as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the person is an affected person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person affected by the use of an AI system?
      `the person's place` IS A `Place of a party` @desc Are you located in the Union, or in a third country?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under Article 16, as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me on the date asked` MEANS
    `Art 2(1)(g) the Regulation applies to the affected person in the Union` `the date asked` `the person is an affected person` `the person's place`

§ `Article 26`

@export Under Article 26(7), as a person affected by an AI system, has the deployer, as an employer, informed the workers' representatives and the affected workers before putting into service or using a high-risk AI system at the workplace?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) and related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if you do not know of such a product.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where the AI system is high-risk because of Article 6(1), does the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations that give an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights than the requirement or obligation the question is about? Answer no if you do not know.
      `limiting the requirement or obligation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would limiting the requirement or obligation the question is about leave the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation unreduced? Answer no if you do not know.
      `the deployer is an employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the deployer is an employer?
      `the high-risk AI system is to be put into service or used at the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the high-risk AI system is to be put into service or used at the workplace?
      `the deployer has informed the workers' representatives and the affected workers that they will be subject to the use of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the deployer has informed the workers' representatives and the affected workers that they will be subject to the use of the high-risk AI system?
      `there are rules and procedures laid down in Union and national law and practice on information of workers and their representatives` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that there are rules and procedures laid down in Union and national law and practice on information of workers and their representatives?
      `the information is provided in accordance with those rules and procedures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the information is provided in accordance with those rules and procedures?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under Article 26(7), as a person affected by an AI system, has the deployer, as an employer, informed the workers' representatives and the affected workers before putting into service or using a high-risk AI system at the workplace` MEANS
    `Art 26(7) the deployer that is an employer has informed the workers' representatives and the affected workers` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` `the deployer is an employer` `the high-risk AI system is to be put into service or used at the workplace` `the deployer has informed the workers' representatives and the affected workers that they will be subject to the use of the high-risk AI system` `there are rules and procedures laid down in Union and national law and practice on information of workers and their representatives` `the information is provided in accordance with those rules and procedures`
    WHERE
        `the AI system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
        `the circumstances` MEANS `Section 3 circumstances` WITH
            `related to Section B products` IS `the AI system is related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
            `Section A equivalent protection` IS `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection`
            `no reduction of the overall level of protection` IS `limiting the requirement or obligation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`

