    `Art 50(1) the provider must ensure that the natural persons concerned are informed that they are interacting with an AI system` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the AI system is intended to interact directly with natural persons` `this is obvious from the point of view of a natural person who is reasonably well-informed, observant and circumspect, taking into account the circumstances and the context of use` `the AI system is authorised by law to detect, prevent, investigate or prosecute criminal offences` `that authorisation is subject to appropriate safeguards for the rights and freedoms of third parties` `the AI system is available for the public to report a criminal offence` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
