      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the paragraph of Article 50 the information is referred to in` IS A NUMBER @desc Give the number: the paragraph of Article 50 the information is referred to in.
      `the date the information was provided` IS A DATE @desc Give the date: the date the information was provided.
      `the date of the first interaction or exposure` IS A DATE @desc Give the date: the date of the first interaction or exposure.
      `the information was provided in a clear and distinguishable manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information was provided in a clear and distinguishable manner?
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if the AI system is not high-risk because of Article 6(1).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 50(5), as a person affected by an AI system, was the information given to me provided in a clear and distinguishable manner at the latest at the time of my first interaction or exposure` IS
    `Art 50(5) the information was provided in a clear and distinguishable manner at the latest at the time of the first interaction or exposure` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the paragraph of Article 50 the information is referred to in` `the date the information was provided` `the date of the first interaction or exposure` `the information was provided in a clear and distinguishable manner` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
    WHERE
        `the AI system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`

-- Article 50(5): Art 50(5) the information conforms to the applicable accessibility requirements
@export Under Article 50(5), as a person affected by an AI system, does the information given to me conform to the applicable accessibility requirements?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the information conforms to the applicable accessibility requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information conforms to the applicable accessibility requirements?
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if the AI system is not high-risk because of Article 6(1).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 50(5), as a person affected by an AI system, does the information given to me conform to the applicable accessibility requirements` IS
    `Art 50(5) the information conforms to the applicable accessibility requirements` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the information conforms to the applicable accessibility requirements` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
    WHERE
        `the AI system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`

-- Article 50: Art 50 the AI system falls under Article 50
@export Under Article 50, as a person affected by an AI system, is the AI system one of the kinds of AI system that Article 50 names?
GIVEN `the AI system is intended to interact directly with natural persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the AI system is intended to interact directly with natural persons?
      `the AI system generates synthetic audio, image, video or text content` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the AI system generates synthetic audio, image, video or text content?
      `the AI system is an emotion recognition system or a biometric categorisation system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the AI system is an emotion recognition system or a biometric categorisation system?
      `the AI system generates or manipulates image, audio or video content constituting a deep fake, or text published with the purpose of informing the public on matters of public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the AI system generates or manipulates image, audio or video content constituting a deep fake, or text published with the purpose of informing the public on matters of public interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 50, as a person affected by an AI system, is the AI system one of the kinds of AI system that Article 50 names` IS
    JUST (`Art 50 the AI system falls under Article 50` `the AI system is intended to interact directly with natural persons` `the AI system generates synthetic audio, image, video or text content` `the AI system is an emotion recognition system or a biometric categorisation system` `the AI system generates or manipulates image, audio or video content constituting a deep fake, or text published with the purpose of informing the public on matters of public interest`)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat person from part P7 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P7-seat-person: THE SEAT LAYER for a person affected by an AI system, over the layer-1 modules of Articles 57 to 71 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act
-- (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744).
-- SEAT: a person affected by an AI system. In this part that is chiefly the SUBJECT of testing in real world conditions (Articles 60 and 61), the DATA SUBJECT whose personal
-- data are processed in an AI regulatory sandbox (Article 59), and a member of the public who consults the EU database (Article 71). Chapter VII (Articles 64 to 70) addresses officials only, so this seat has no
-- question for the group of Chapter VII. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question calls one layer-1 function.
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs: a yes/no, a date, a number, each with an @desc. The date asked comes first. The provision group `General` (Chapter VI and Chapter VIII) applies from 2 August 2026.
-- Commencement is IN for this Regulation (assumed, not ruled). The text is the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026, a rendering with no legal effect.

§ `Under Article 57: the group General`

-- The applicability question for the provision group `General` that Article 57 opens in this part's range: it asks only the date, and passes the core's constants for the route, the placement date and the change.
@export Under Article 57, as a person affected by an AI system, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 57, as a person affected by an AI system, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `General` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)


§ `Under Article 59: personal data processed in an AI regulatory sandbox`

-- This question arises only if your personal data were lawfully collected for other purposes and are processed in a sandbox.

-- Article 59(1)(f), one of the ten conditions of processing in the sandbox.
@export Under Article 59, as a person affected by an AI system, is the processing of my personal data in the AI regulatory sandbox one that neither leads to measures or decisions affecting me nor affects my data protection rights?
GIVEN `the processing leads to no measures or decisions affecting the data subjects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the processing leads to no measures or decisions affecting the data subjects? Answer yes or no.
      `the processing does not affect the application of their rights laid down in Union law on the protection of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the processing does not affect the application of their rights laid down in Union law on the protection of personal data? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 59, as a person affected by an AI system, is the processing of my personal data in the AI regulatory sandbox one that neither leads to measures or decisions affecting me nor affects my data protection rights` IS
    `Art 59(1)(f) the processing neither leads to measures or decisions affecting the data subjects nor affects their rights` `the processing leads to no measures or decisions affecting the data subjects` `the processing does not affect the application of their rights laid down in Union law on the protection of personal data`


§ `Under Article 60: testing in real world conditions`

-- These questions arise only if you take part in testing of an AI system in real world conditions, or are the legal representative of someone who does.

-- Article 60(5), first sentence: a subject, or their legally designated representative as appropriate, may withdraw at any time, without detriment and without having to give a justification.
@export Under Article 60, as a person affected by an AI system, may I withdraw from the testing in real world conditions at any time by revoking my informed consent?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the person is a subject of the testing in real world conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a subject of testing in real world conditions of an AI system?
      `the person is the subject's legally designated representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the legally designated representative of a subject of such testing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 60, as a person affected by an AI system, may I withdraw from the testing in real world conditions at any time by revoking my informed consent` IS
    `Art 60(5) the subject may withdraw from the testing by revoking the informed consent` `the date asked` `the person is a subject of the testing in real world conditions` `the person is the subject's legally designated representative`

-- Article 60(5), first sentence.
@export Under Article 60, as a person affected by an AI system, may I request the immediate and permanent deletion of my personal data collected in the testing?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the person is a subject of the testing in real world conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a subject of testing in real world conditions of an AI system?
      `the person is the subject's legally designated representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the legally designated representative of a subject of such testing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 60, as a person affected by an AI system, may I request the immediate and permanent deletion of my personal data collected in the testing` IS
    `Art 60(5) the subject may request the immediate and permanent deletion of their personal data` `the date asked` `the person is a subject of the testing in real world conditions` `the person is the subject's legally designated representative`

-- Article 60(5): the withdrawal is without any resulting detriment and without having to provide any justification. JUST FALSE means the text says no.
@export Under Article 60, as a person affected by an AI system, if I am required to give a justification for my withdrawal, or I suffer a detriment because I withdraw, is that allowed by the Regulation?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the subject is required to provide a justification for the withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required to provide a justification for your withdrawal?
      `the subject suffers a detriment resulting from the withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you suffer a detriment as a result of your withdrawal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 60, as a person affected by an AI system, if I am required to give a justification for my withdrawal, or I suffer a detriment because I withdraw, is that allowed by the Regulation` IS
    `Art 60(5) the subject is required to justify the withdrawal or suffers a detriment from it` `the date asked` `the subject is required to provide a justification for the withdrawal` `the subject suffers a detriment resulting from the withdrawal`

-- Article 60(5), second sentence: the withdrawal does not affect the activities already carried out. JUST FALSE means the text says no.
@export Under Article 60, as a person affected by an AI system, does my withdrawal of consent affect the activities already carried out?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the activities were carried out before the withdrawal of the informed consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the activities were carried out before the withdrawal of the informed consent? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 60, as a person affected by an AI system, does my withdrawal of consent affect the activities already carried out` IS
    `Art 60(5) the withdrawal of the informed consent affects the activities already carried out` `the date asked` `the activities were carried out before the withdrawal of the informed consent`

-- Article 60(4)(g): a condition of the provider's testing.
@export Under Article 60, as a person affected by an AI system, if I belong to a vulnerable group because of my age or disability, am I appropriately protected in the testing?
GIVEN `some of the subjects of the testing belong to vulnerable groups due to their age or disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that some of the subjects of the testing belong to vulnerable groups due to their age or disability? Answer yes or no.
      `those subjects are appropriately protected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that those subjects are appropriately protected? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 60, as a person affected by an AI system, if I belong to a vulnerable group because of my age or disability, am I appropriately protected in the testing` IS
    `Art 60(4)(g) the subjects who belong to vulnerable groups are appropriately protected` `some of the subjects of the testing belong to vulnerable groups due to their age or disability` `those subjects are appropriately protected`


§ `Under Article 61: informed consent`

-- Article 61(1)(a) to (e): the nature and objectives; the conditions and duration; your rights and guarantees; how to request the reversal of the decisions of the AI system; the identification number and the contact details.
@export Under Article 61, as a person affected by an AI system, was I informed of all the matters Article 61(1) lists before I agreed to take part?
GIVEN `the subject has been informed of the nature and objectives of the testing in real world conditions and the possible inconvenience that may be linked to their participation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the subject has been informed of the nature and objectives of the testing in real world conditions and the possible inconvenience that may be linked to their participation? Answer yes or no.
      `the subject has been informed of the conditions under which the testing is to be conducted, including the expected duration of the subject or subjects’ participation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the subject has been informed of the conditions under which the testing is to be conducted, including the expected duration of the subject or subjects’ participation? Answer yes or no.
      `the subject has been informed of their rights, and the guarantees regarding their participation, in particular their right to refuse to participate in, and the right to withdraw from, testing at any time without any resulting detriment and without having to provide any justification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the subject has been informed of their rights, and the guarantees regarding their participation, in particular their right to refuse to participate in, and the right to withdraw from, testing at any time without any resulting detriment and without having to provide any justification? Answer yes or no.
      `the subject has been informed of the arrangements for requesting the reversal or the disregarding of the predictions, recommendations or decisions of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the subject has been informed of the arrangements for requesting the reversal or the disregarding of the predictions, recommendations or decisions of the AI system? Answer yes or no.
      `the subject has been informed of the Union-wide unique single identification number of the testing in accordance with Article 60(4) point (c), and the contact details of the provider or its legal representative from whom further information can be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the subject has been informed of the Union-wide unique single identification number of the testing in accordance with Article 60(4) point (c), and the contact details of the provider or its legal representative from whom further information can be obtained? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 61, as a person affected by an AI system, was I informed of all the matters Article 61(1) lists before I agreed to take part` IS
    `Art 61(1) the subject has been informed of all the matters listed` `the subject has been informed of the nature and objectives of the testing in real world conditions and the possible inconvenience that may be linked to their participation` `the subject has been informed of the conditions under which the testing is to be conducted, including the expected duration of the subject or subjects’ participation` `the subject has been informed of their rights, and the guarantees regarding their participation, in particular their right to refuse to participate in, and the right to withdraw from, testing at any time without any resulting detriment and without having to provide any justification` `the subject has been informed of the arrangements for requesting the reversal or the disregarding of the predictions, recommendations or decisions of the AI system` `the subject has been informed of the Union-wide unique single identification number of the testing in accordance with Article 60(4) point (c), and the contact details of the provider or its legal representative from whom further information can be obtained`

-- Article 61(1), lead.
@export Under Article 61, as a person affected by an AI system, was my freely-given informed consent obtained before my participation in the testing?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the testing is testing in real world conditions under Article 60` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the testing is testing in real world conditions under Article 60? Answer yes or no.
      `the consent is freely given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the consent is freely given? Answer yes or no.
      `the subject was duly informed with concise, clear, relevant, and understandable information regarding the matters listed in points (a) to (e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the subject was duly informed with concise, clear, relevant, and understandable information regarding the matters listed in points (a) to (e)? Answer yes or no.
      `the consent was obtained prior to the subject's participation in the testing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the consent was obtained prior to the subject's participation in the testing? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 61, as a person affected by an AI system, was my freely-given informed consent obtained before my participation in the testing` IS
    `Art 61(1) freely-given informed consent has been obtained from the subject prior to their participation` `the date asked` `the testing is testing in real world conditions under Article 60` `the consent is freely given` `the subject was duly informed with concise, clear, relevant, and understandable information regarding the matters listed in points (a) to (e)` `the consent was obtained prior to the subject's participation in the testing`

-- Article 61(2).
@export Under Article 61, as a person affected by an AI system, was my consent dated and documented, and was a copy given to me or to my legal representative?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the informed consent is dated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the informed consent is dated? Answer yes or no.
      `the informed consent is documented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the informed consent is documented? Answer yes or no.
      `a copy is given to the subjects of testing or their legal representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a copy is given to the subjects of testing or their legal representative? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 61, as a person affected by an AI system, was my consent dated and documented, and was a copy given to me or to my legal representative` IS
    `Art 61(2) the informed consent has been dated and documented and a copy given` `the date asked` `the informed consent is dated` `the informed consent is documented` `a copy is given to the subjects of testing or their legal representative`


§ `Under Article 71: the EU database`

-- These questions arise only if you consult the EU database, or your personal data are in it.

-- Article 71(4), first sentence: with the exception of the secure section referred to in Article 49(4) and Article 60(4), point (c).
@export Under Article 71, as a person affected by an AI system, is the information in the EU database about a registered AI system accessible to me, publicly and in a user-friendly manner?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the information is registered in accordance with Article 49` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information is registered in accordance with Article 49? Answer yes or no.
      `the information is not in the section referred to in Article 49(4) and Article 60(4), point (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information is not in the section referred to in Article 49(4) and Article 60(4), point (c)? Answer yes or no.
      `the information is accessible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information is accessible? Answer yes or no.
      `the information is publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information is publicly available? Answer yes or no.
      `the information is accessible and publicly available in a user-friendly manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the information is accessible and publicly available in a user-friendly manner? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 71, as a person affected by an AI system, is the information in the EU database about a registered AI system accessible to me, publicly and in a user-friendly manner` IS
    `Art 71(4) the information registered in accordance with Article 49 is accessible and publicly available in a user-friendly manner` `the date asked` `the information is registered in accordance with Article 49` `the information is not in the section referred to in Article 49(4) and Article 60(4), point (c)` `the information is accessible` `the information is publicly available` `the information is accessible and publicly available in a user-friendly manner`

-- Article 71(4), third sentence: accessible only to market surveillance authorities and the Commission, unless the prospective provider or provider has given consent for also making the information accessible to the public.
@export Under Article 71, as a person affected by an AI system, may I, as a member of the public, access the information registered for testing in real world conditions under Article 60, given whether the provider has consented?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the prospective provider or provider has given consent for also making the information accessible to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the provider or prospective provider given consent for making the information registered for the testing accessible to the public?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 71, as a person affected by an AI system, may I, as a member of the public, access the information registered for testing in real world conditions under Article 60, given whether the provider has consented` IS
    `Art 71(4) the person may access the information registered in accordance with Article 60` `the date asked` FALSE FALSE `the prospective provider or provider has given consent for also making the information accessible to the public`

-- Article 71(5), first sentence.
@export Under Article 71, as a person affected by an AI system, does the EU database hold personal data about me only in so far as necessary for collecting and processing information under the Regulation?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the personal data are necessary for collecting and processing information in accordance with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the personal data are necessary for collecting and processing information in accordance with this Regulation? Answer yes or no.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 71, as a person affected by an AI system, does the EU database hold personal data about me only in so far as necessary for collecting and processing information under the Regulation` IS
    `Art 71(5) the EU database contains personal data only in so far as necessary for collecting and processing information in accordance with this Regulation` `the date asked` `the personal data are necessary for collecting and processing information in accordance with this Regulation`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat person from part P8 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P8 seat layer: a person affected by an AI system: what the powers and duties of the authorities in Articles 77 and 79 mean for the person.
-- SEAT: a person affected by an AI system
--
-- Nothing here is new law: each question calls the layer-1 function of Articles 72 to 79 (P8-art72 to P8-art79) that answers it, and the keel
-- (aia-definitions, aia-timeline, aia-core) for the role facts and the dates. Every question takes plain inputs: a yes/no, a date, a number or
-- one of the keel's own choices, each with an @desc worded for the person asking. A question answers JUST value, or NOTHING where the text does
-- not decide it (the Regulation does not apply yet on the date asked, or the text is silent); a JUST FALSE is a "no" the text itself gives.
-- The seat assumes its role: the keel handed to this part has no function for it (the role is Article 2(1)(e) / (g), which the keel's scope module
-- would own), so there is no role question and the person asking is taken to be a person affected by an AI system, located in the Union.
-- Questions are grouped by Article in the order of the text; the role question and the applicability questions come first.


§ `Which provisions apply on the date asked`

-- Calls the gate helper of P8-gate, which passes the group to the keel's `Art 113 the provision group applies`.
@export Under Article 72, as a person affected by an AI system, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 72, as a person affected by an AI system, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)

§ `Article 77: Powers of authorities protecting fundamental rights and cooperation with market surveillance authorities`
-- Arises only if a high-risk AI system referred to in Annex III is used and an authority protecting fundamental rights is involved.

-- Calls `Art 77(1) the national public authority or body has the power to request and access the information or documentation`.
@export Under Article 77(1), as a person affected by an AI system, can the national public authority protecting fundamental rights request and access the documentation on the high-risk AI system that affects me?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the authority or body supervises or enforces the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the authority or body supervises or enforces the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights?
      `the supervision or enforcement is in relation to the use of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the supervision or enforcement is in relation to the use of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III?
      `access to the information or documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling the mandate of the authority or body within the limits of its jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that access to the information or documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling the mandate of the authority or body within the limits of its jurisdiction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 77(1), as a person affected by an AI system, can the national public authority protecting fundamental rights request and access the documentation on the high-risk AI system that affects me` IS
    `Art 77(1) the national public authority or body has the power to request and access the information or documentation` `the date asked` `the authority or body supervises or enforces the respect of obligations under Union law protecting fundamental rights` `the supervision or enforcement is in relation to the use of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III` `access to the information or documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling the mandate of the authority or body within the limits of its jurisdiction`

§ `Article 79: Procedure at national level for dealing with AI systems presenting a risk`
-- Arises only if a market surveillance authority has found that an AI system presents a risk.

-- Calls `Art 79(2) second sentence particular attention is given to the AI system presenting a risk to vulnerable groups`.
@export Under Article 79(2), as a person affected by an AI system, must particular attention be given to an AI system presenting a risk to vulnerable groups?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the AI system presents a risk to vulnerable groups` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the AI system presents a risk to vulnerable groups?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 79(2), as a person affected by an AI system, must particular attention be given to an AI system presenting a risk to vulnerable groups` IS
